  D = 1,2,3 give NO integer s  =>  the interval FORCES D >= 4.
  (boxeph-S123's stratification gave D >= 3 for the wider Farey interval;
   the attained interval (1/14,3/41) pushes it one step further.)

  total candidate (D,s) pairs with D <= 15: 30
  first few: [(4, 55), (5, 69), (6, 83), (7, 96), (7, 97), (8, 110), (8, 111), (9, 124)]

  Note the list is INFINITE (D unbounded), since s ~ 14D always admits
  an integer once D >= 4.  So emptiness cannot be settled by finite check
  alone -- it needs an argument that bounds D for a realising family.

HUNTING the mediant 4/55 and anything else inside (1/14, 3/41)
  Farey: |1*41 - 3*14| = 1, so 1/14 and 3/41 are NEIGHBOURS and
  4/55 = (1+3)/(14+41) is the unique least-denominator fraction inside.

  10895 families tested (residue-band at s=55, plus {1..11,x,y} shapes)
  families with M strictly inside (1/14, 3/41): 0
  NONE -- including no realisation of the mediant 4/55
